# THE FRONTEND'S BUILD ARTEFACTS — not web/ itself. `web/.dockerignore` does NOT cover
# these: it applies only to the frontend service, whose build context is ./web. The root
# Dockerfile builds from `.`, so without these lines 297MB of node_modules across ~50k
# small files is packed into the build context. That is what turns "exporting to image"
# into a 20-minute step on Docker Desktop for Windows, where every one of those files
# crosses the WSL2 filesystem boundary.
#
# web/ SOURCE must stay in the context: the root Dockerfile's `ui` stage builds the SPA
# there for the single-container deployment (see Settings.static_dir). It runs its own
# `npm ci` from the lockfile, so a host node_modules would be ignored anyway.
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/.angular/

# The legacy Chroma directory. Chroma was removed in P2 (retrieval moved to Postgres +
# pgvector), so this is 39MB of dead weight that would otherwise ship in every image.
vector_store/

# Local eval/test artefacts — regenerated, never read by the running service.
.ruff_cache
htmlcov
scripts/

__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python
env
venv
.venv
pip-log.txt
pip-delete-this-directory.txt
.tox
.coverage
.coverage.*
.cache
nosetests.xml
coverage.xml
*.cover
*.log
.git
.gitignore
.mypy_cache
.pytest_cache
.hypotheses
test_api.ipynb
LOG_FILE
